Given a directory of images, the gallery should dynamically fit every image into a defined boundary.
Line of processing:
    - Load the images
    - Get their aspect ratios
    - Calculate an appropriate height for each row
    - Calculate each image's width from its aspect ratio
    - Create the DOM
    - Recalculate or use preset calculations when the container resizes

First Step : Loading the images
    - Create the collage class
    - Rander the images to the collage container

Implementation:
    - Each image in this machine will be know by the following format:
        - {<directory/url>, <alt_text>}
        - a list of images will be passed at intialisation(to the constructor method).
        - a render method will take each of the images and append them to the container.

Every image seems to have its own resolution and aspect ratio.
We need a common limit, width of every photo = height * aspect ratio.
This will maintain their natural width while scaling down to fit desired orientations.

With consideration of the gaping, each image will adapt to the max width ratio of the container.

Second Step: Adaptive loading
    - Implement a function that calculates the ratio for each image